  "notes": "Official Wake Forest University 2026-2027 Academic Bulletin, Psychology B.A. requirements. The catalog publishes degree requirements with no official semester sequence — collected as a single requirements block per coordinator 2026-10-09 convention. Major requires minimum 32 hours in Psychology across 3 tiers. Tier 1: PSY 151 (3), PSY 211/211L (4), PSY 212/212L (4). Tier 2: at least 3 credits from each of three Perspectives — recorded as three 3-credit choice slots at the tier minimum; 'Brief Topics' options (PSY 239, 259, 279) carry 1.5 credits per the bulletin course descriptions. PSY 247 appears in two Perspectives; the bulletin states a course in more than one group may satisfy either perspective but not both. Tier 3: 3 credits Seminar in Psychology; 6 credits Research in Psychology, of which students may replace 3 with 3 credits from Experiences in Psychology — recorded as two 3-credit choice slots at the minimum. A 3-credit psychology elective block brings the plan to the 32-hour minimum. Per-course credits verified against the bulletin's PSY course descriptions.",
